# rule.always.weigh-a-read-by-what-it-rules-out

> **a read confirms a claim only as far as it rules out the rival claims. name the rival; if the read would look the same under it, the read carries no weight.**

move: name the claim and one rival (spin more than one hypothesis) · per read, ask: would it differ under the rival? · count only reads that differ · seek the read that would disprove your claim (Heuer).
test: **name the rival claim. would this read have looked any different under it?**
blocker: a claim reported as confirmed, which a peer acted on, on reads that would look the same under a named rival
nitpick: a diagnosis that names no rival claim
